# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover. The whole folder is ignored: what it holds is per-machine module,
# interpreter and inspection config, not shared state. The JetBrains template
# that would track part of it is at
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
.idea/

# Spike fixtures are throwaway git repos; results are raw measurement data.
spikes/fixtures/

# spikes/results/ moved to D:/repos/redkiln-corpus at the pin in CORPUS_PIN
# (ADR-0013). Charter §14.2 still makes the raw records a deliverable — they are
# a deliverable OF THE CORPUS REPO now, and AC-465 forbids them here.

# Python bytecode from the spike tooling (spikes/p1, p2, p9). The .py sources
# are tracked; the caches are per-interpreter and rebuild on every run.
__pycache__/

# Regenerable census output of the 2026-09-10 audit instrument (references/audit/2026-09-10/scripts/); ~16 MB, rebuilt by the scripts
references/audit/2026-09-10/census/
references/audit/2026-09-10/rerun/
references/audit/2026-09-10/scripts/__pycache__/

# Waiter logs, tee'd for the `until grep` waiters. The JSONL in spikes/results/ is the evidence.
spikes/*.log

# Suspended graph state; regenerable, and meaningless without the run that made it.
# The digests that matter are in spikes/results/p8.jsonl.
spikes/results/p8-state/

# Extra build dirs cut when target/ was locked by a live run.
spikes/runner/target-*/

# Step 7c (s7c §7c.14): the predecessor checkout AC-334's real-toolchain flip materialises ONCE, locally, from
# the pinned bundle -- under target/, which the first row already ignores; this row names the intent.
target/predecessor-*/

spikes/corpus/
spikes/runner/
spikes/results/*
!spikes/results/instrument-checks/
spikes/results/instrument-checks/*
!spikes/results/instrument-checks/RUNBOOK-instrument.txt

# Written by the Claude Code `redkiln` PLUGIN, not by this workspace: session_start /
# session_end rows keyed by actor+worktree+branch. No crate here writes it -- grep over
# crates/ for `telemetry` finds only event-kind prose. `.redkiln/` is tracked as of Step 7e,
# so without this row a foreign tool dirties the tree between a stage's two close commits.
# [Step 8, 2026-09-21]
.redkiln/telemetry/
